    '|b||Granted, the machine runs on rivalry and markups, and its growth dwarfs the triangles. Now here''s its bill.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6600
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Every year American employers lay off about twenty million workers. That was 2024, a good year.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:p5hq69'
    '|b||Most find new work, but some never recover. Long-serving Pennsylvania workers laid off in the 1980s still earned about a quarter less five years on.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1em98d'
    '|a||So churn does hurt, and for a long time. I strike my own claim.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:my2qfd'
    '|a||But stop the churn and you stop the gains. In American retail in the 1990s, nearly all the productivity growth came from new, better stores replacing old ones.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1cmajcf'
    '|b||Then here''s my strongest point. Static waste isn''t only little triangles. Hsieh and Klenow estimated that moving workers and machines to the best firms, as in America, would raise factory productivity by 30 to 50 percent in China and 40 to 60 in India.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 16000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:l0dfwi'
    '|a||Which is the twist: that moving is churn too. Fixing today''s waste and growing tomorrow run through the same exits and entries.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:9l9g7h'
    '|a||How sure are we? That over decades growth matters more than the triangles: mostly agreed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ywjxgm'
    '|b||Whether the growth is worth the lost jobs, and who should carry them: that''s a question of values, and contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1heczip'
    '|b||Three new cases. A government caps every drug''s price at the cost of making one more pill. What happens over twenty years?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7520
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:19xnyf8'
    '|b||Cheaper pills now, fewer new drugs later: with price at marginal cost, nothing is left to pay for the research.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Harbourtown''s boatyard closes after a mainland rival builds better boats. What follows?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||The town can gain overall while the yard''s workers lose for years: buyers get better boats, but displaced workers often earn less long after.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10560
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||A town bans big-box stores to protect its small shops. Going by the retail evidence, what happens to the town''s retail productivity?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||It grows more slowly: in 1990s American retail, new, better stores replacing old ones brought nearly all the productivity growth.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||So which efficiency matters more in the long run? The growing pie, almost surely; but whether markets work also depends on how they treat the people the machine runs over.':
